To write and execute a Python program to implement different types of data visualizations using Matplotlib and Pandas libraries.
2. Algorithm
Start the program.
Import Pandas and Matplotlib libraries.
Create a DataFrame containing Month and Sales.
Create a line plot using plt.plot().
Add title and axis labels.
Create a bar plot using plt.bar().
Create a scatter plot using plt.scatter().
Create a histogram using plt.hist().
Create a pie chart using plt.pie().
Display each graph using plt.show().
Stop the program.
3. Source Code

import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Sample Data
df = pd.DataFrame({
    "Month": ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr"],
    "Sales": [200, 250, 300, 290]
})

# 1. Line Plot
plt.figure()
plt.plot(df["Month"], df["Sales"])
plt.title("Line Plot - Monthly Sales")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Sales")
plt.show()

# 2. Bar Plot
plt.figure()
plt.bar(df["Month"], df["Sales"])
plt.title("Bar Plot - Monthly Sales")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Sales")
plt.show()

# 3. Scatter Plot
plt.figure()
plt.scatter(df["Month"], df["Sales"])
plt.title("Scatter Plot - Monthly Sales")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Sales")
plt.show()

# 4. Histogram
plt.figure()
plt.hist(df["Sales"])
plt.title("Histogram - Sales Distribution")
plt.xlabel("Sales")
plt.ylabel("Frequency")
plt.show()

# 5. Pie Chart
plt.figure()
plt.pie(df["Sales"], labels=df["Month"],
        autopct="%1.1f%%")
plt.title("Pie Chart - Sales Share")
plt.show()

